cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  qml-trojan-benchmark: Security of Quantum Machine Learning
  against trojan/backdoor insertion
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it using
  the metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Daniel
    family-names: Ramon
    email: 81169421+DanielRamon10@users.noreply.github.com
repository-code: 'https://github.com/DanielRamon10/qml-trojan-benchmark'
url: 'https://github.com/DanielRamon10/qml-trojan-benchmark'
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, laptop-scale benchmark studying the security of
  variational quantum classifiers (VQCs) against trojan/backdoor
  insertion by a compromised quantum software-supply-chain component
  (a malicious Qiskit transpiler pass). It bridges trojan detection in
  quantum circuits and Quantum Adversarial Machine Learning (QAML),
  measuring the behavioural and classification-accuracy impact of
  single-gate insertions (TVD/BC/BD vs a sampling baseline), a
  triggered conditional backdoor (attack success rate vs clean
  accuracy), and text-based (BoW/TF-IDF) detection of infected circuits.
keywords:
  - quantum machine learning
  - quantum adversarial machine learning
  - hardware trojan
  - backdoor attack
  - variational quantum classifier
  - software supply chain security
  - Qiskit
  - OpenQASM
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-10-07'
